From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: the hot item and inactive text of Windows 7's menu bars

Purpose: draw themed menu bars as Windows 7 does when the mouse is over
them and when their window is inactive.
Windows behavior: while the window is active and no menu is open, the
bar item under the mouse is drawn with MENU_BARITEM's hot state; an
inactive window's bar has no hot item and gray text (109,109,109).
Wine before: the bar item was drawn only when pushed, and the text kept
the active color.
Change: DefWindowProc's WM_NCMOUSEMOVE and WM_NCMOUSELEAVE follow the
bar item under the mouse (TME_NONCLIENT | TME_LEAVE) and redraw it with
MBI_HOT or MBI_DISABLEDHOT; selecting a bar item clears it. An inactive
bar's items use the disabled text color.
Evidence: w7cmp.exe on Windows 7 and in the session, the mouse over a
bar item of the active window and of an inactive one, and moved into
the client area: the same as Windows 7 apart from the known glyph
differences.
Scope: themed menus (the Windows 7 shell with a version 4 visual style).
---
 dlls/win32u/defwnd.c         |  5 +++++
 dlls/win32u/menu.c           | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
index 42fc315..f807738 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -2494,6 +2494,10 @@ static LRESULT handle_nc_mouse_move( HWND hwnd, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam )
 
     TRACE( "hwnd=%p wparam=%#lx lparam=%#lx\n", hwnd, (long)wparam, lparam );
 
+    pt.x = (short)LOWORD( lparam );
+    pt.y = (short)HIWORD( lparam );
+    track_menu_bar_hot_item( hwnd, wparam == HTMENU ? &pt : NULL );
+
     if (wparam != HTHSCROLL && wparam != HTVSCROLL)
         return 0;
 
@@ -2515,6 +2519,7 @@ static LRESULT handle_nc_mouse_leave( HWND hwnd )
 
     TRACE( "hwnd=%p\n", hwnd );
 
+    track_menu_bar_hot_item( hwnd, NULL );
     if (style & WS_HSCROLL)
         handle_scroll_event( hwnd, SB_HORZ, WM_NCMOUSELEAVE, pt );
     if (style & WS_VSCROLL)
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/menu.c b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
